{"course": {"id": "s16", "title": "Camday – Cambridge Primary Mathematics — Stage 6", "units": [{"n": 1, "t": "The Number System"}, {"n": 2, "t": "Numbers and Sequences"}, {"n": 3, "t": "Averages"}, {"n": 4, "t": "Addition and Subtraction (1)"}, {"n": 5, "t": "2D Shapes"}, {"n": 6, "t": "Fractions and Percentages"}, {"n": 7, "t": "Exploring Measures"}, {"n": 8, "t": "Addition and Subtraction (2)"}, {"n": 9, "t": "Probability"}, {"n": 10, "t": "Multiplication and Division (1)"}, {"n": 11, "t": "3D Shapes"}, {"n": 12, "t": "Ratio and Proportion"}, {"n": 13, "t": "Angles"}, {"n": 14, "t": "Multiplication and Division (2)"}, {"n": 15, "t": "Data"}, {"n": 16, "t": "The Laws of Arithmetic"}, {"n": 17, "t": "Transformations"}]}, "unit": {"n": 12, "stage": 16, "title": "Ratio and Proportion", "strandShort": "Number", "blurb": "Using ratio to compare parts with parts, proportion to compare parts with the whole, and solving direct proportion problems.", "strand": "Number", "framework": "Cambridge Primary Mathematics (0096), Stage 6", "lesson": true, "subject": "maths", "read": "media/read/m6u12.pdf"}, "objectives": {"O1": {"code": "6Nf.07", "sec": "12.1", "codeNote": "", "t": "Understand ratio as a part-to-part comparison and write and simplify ratios."}, "O2": {"code": "6Nf.08", "sec": "12.2", "codeNote": "", "t": "Understand direct proportion and use it to solve problems, including recipes and prices."}}, "sections": [{"id": "12.1", "title": "Ratio", "objs": ["O1"], "lesson": [{"k": "hook", "t": "Fruit punch", "p": ["A fruit punch recipe uses **2 cups of orange juice for every 3 cups of apple juice**. Lily makes a big bowl with **8 cups of orange**.", "How much apple juice does she need? Try it before you read on."]}, {"k": "recall", "t": "Times tables", "p": ["Multiples of 2: 2, 4, 6, 8; of 3: 3, 6, 9, 12."], "qq": {"id": "m6u12s1t01", "type": "num", "prompt": "2 × 4 = 8. What is 3 × 4?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 12, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "12."}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "What a ratio is", "p": ["A **ratio** compares amounts: orange : apple = **2 : 3** ('2 to 3'). Order matters: apple : orange = 3 : 2.", "**Equivalent ratios** are made by multiplying (or dividing) both parts by the same number: 2 : 3 = 4 : 6 = 6 : 9 = **8 : 12**."], "table": {"head": ["Orange", "2", "4", "6", "8"], "rows": [["Apple", "3", "6", "9", "12"]]}, "p2": ["Lily needs **12 cups** of apple juice."]}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Simplest form", "p": ["Divide both parts by their **highest common factor**: 12 : 18 → ÷ 6 → **2 : 3**.", "A ratio is in simplest form when the parts have no common factor except 1."]}, {"k": "try", "t": "Equivalent", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m6u12s1t02", "type": "num", "prompt": "2 : 3 = 10 : ?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 15, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "× 5.", "reason": "15."}}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I work with ratios?", "p": ["Step 1: Write the parts in the right order.", "Step 2: Equivalent: multiply or divide both parts by the same number.", "Step 3: Simplest form: divide by the highest common factor.", "Step 4: Check: the ratio should still describe the same mix."]}, {"k": "example", "t": "Simplify", "p": [], "q": "Simplify 15 : 25.", "steps": [["÷ 5", ""]], "a": "3 : 5"}, {"k": "example", "t": "From a picture", "p": [], "q": "A bead pattern has 6 red and 9 blue beads. Red : blue in simplest form?", "steps": [["6 : 9 → ÷ 3", ""]], "a": "2 : 3"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Find a part", "p": [], "q": "Boys : girls = 4 : 5. There are 20 girls. Boys?", "steps": [["5 × 4 = 20", ""], ["4 × 4 = 16", ""]], "a": "16"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Three parts", "p": [], "q": "Simplify 6 : 12 : 18.", "steps": [["÷ 6", ""]], "a": "1 : 2 : 3"}, {"k": "try", "t": "Simplify", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m6u12s1t03", "type": "short", "prompt": "Simplify 14 : 21.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Knowledge", "accept": ["2:3", "2:3", "2 : 3"], "hint": "÷ 7.", "reason": "2 : 3."}}, {"k": "error", "t": "Added instead of multiplied", "p": ["Find the first wrong line."], "q": "Orange : apple = 2 : 3. With 8 cups of orange …", "lines": ["orange went up by 6, so apple = 3 + 6 = 9"], "bad": 0, "why": "Ratios scale by MULTIPLYING: 2 × 4 = 8, so apple = 3 × 4 = 12.", "fix": [["× 4 → 12 cups", ""]], "id": "m6u12s1t04"}, {"k": "mistake", "t": "Adding the same amount to both parts", "p": ["Multiply both parts by the same number."]}, {"k": "tip", "t": "Real life", "p": ["Recipes, paint mixing and maps (1 : 100) all use ratios."]}, {"k": "summary", "t": "What to remember", "p": ["A ratio compares amounts in order.", "Equivalent ratios: multiply or divide both parts.", "Simplest form: divide by the HCF.", "Never add the same number to both parts."]}], "video": {"src": null, "offset": 0, "dur": 720, "range": ""}, "stops": [{"id": "12.1-k1", "t": 1, "after": 0, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m6u12s1k01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Before you read on: cups of apple juice?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 12, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}}, {"id": "12.1-k2", "t": 2, "after": 4, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m6u12s1k02", "type": "num", "prompt": "2 : 3 = 6 : ?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 9, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}}, {"id": "12.1-k3", "t": 3, "after": 9, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m6u12s1k03", "type": "short", "prompt": "Simplify 12 : 18.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Knowledge", "accept": ["2:3", "2:3", "2 : 3"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}}, {"id": "12.1-k4", "t": 4, "after": 14, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m6u12s1k04", "type": "num", "prompt": "Quick check: boys : girls 4 : 5, 20 girls. Boys?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 16, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}}], "captions": [], "chapters": [[0, 300]], "req": [{"id": "m6u12s1r01", "type": "short", "prompt": "Simplify 4 : 8.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Knowledge", "accept": ["1:2", "1:2", "1 : 2"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m6u12s1r02", "type": "short", "prompt": "Simplify 10 : 15.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Knowledge", "accept": ["2:3", "2:3", "2 : 3"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m6u12s1r03", "type": "short", "prompt": "Simplify 18 : 24.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Knowledge", "accept": ["3:4", "3:4", "3 : 4"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m6u12s1r04", "type": "num", "prompt": "1 : 4 = 5 : ?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 20, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m6u12s1r05", "type": "num", "prompt": "3 : 7 = ? : 21", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 9, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m6u12s1r06", "type": "short", "prompt": "5 cats, 8 dogs. Cats : dogs?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Knowledge", "accept": ["5:8", "5:8", "5 : 8"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m6u12s1r07", "type": "short", "prompt": "Simplify 20 : 30 : 50.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Knowledge", "accept": ["2:3:5", "2:3:5", "2 : 3 : 5"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m6u12s1r08", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Equivalent to 3 : 4?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "9 : 12", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "4 : 5", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}], "prac": [{"id": "m6u12s1p01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Paint: blue : white = 1 : 3. 12 tins of white. Blue tins?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 4, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m6u12s1p02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Flour : sugar = 5 : 2. 300 g flour. Sugar (g)?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 120, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m6u12s1p03", "type": "short", "prompt": "A class has 12 boys and 16 girls. Boys : girls simplest?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Knowledge", "accept": ["3:4", "3:4", "3 : 4"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m6u12s1p04", "type": "explain", "prompt": "Is 2 : 5 the same as 5 : 2? Explain with an example.", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "rubric": [{"pt": "no", "kw": ["\\bno\\b|not"]}, {"pt": "order matters example", "kw": ["order|boys|girls|first|cats"]}], "need": 2, "model": "No – order matters: 2 boys to 5 girls is not the same as 5 boys to 2 girls.", "hint": "", "reason": "No – order matters: 2 boys to 5 girls is not the same as 5 boys to 2 girls."}, {"id": "m6u12s1p05", "type": "short", "prompt": "Simplify 45 : 60.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Knowledge", "accept": ["3:4", "3:4", "3 : 4"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m6u12s1p06", "type": "num", "prompt": "Red : green = 3 : 5. 24 green. Red?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 15, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m6u12s1p07", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Which is NOT equivalent to 2 : 6?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "3 : 8", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "1 : 3", "ok": false, "fb": ""}, {"t": "4 : 12", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}, {"id": "m6u12s1p08", "type": "num", "prompt": "Ratio 2 : 3, total 25 sweets. How many in the larger part?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 15, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "5 parts → 5 each.", "reason": ""}], "adv": [{"id": "m6u12s1a01", "type": "num", "prompt": "* Advanced. Share 42 in the ratio 1 : 2 : 3. Largest share?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 21, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m6u12s1a02", "type": "short", "prompt": "* Advanced. Simplify 1.5 : 2.5.", "diff": "VH", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Knowledge", "accept": ["3:5", "3:5", "3 : 5"], "hint": "× 2 first.", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m6u12s1a03", "type": "explain", "prompt": "* Advanced. A recipe for 4 people uses 200 g pasta and 100 g cheese. Explain the ratio and how to make it for 6.", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "rubric": [{"pt": "2 : 1", "kw": ["2 ?: ?1"]}, {"pt": "300 g and 150 g", "kw": ["300|150"]}], "need": 2, "model": "Pasta : cheese = 2 : 1. For 6 people multiply by 1.5: 300 g pasta, 150 g cheese.", "hint": "", "reason": "Pasta : cheese = 2 : 1. For 6 people multiply by 1.5: 300 g pasta, 150 g cheese."}], "more": [{"id": "m6u12s1m01", "type": "short", "prompt": "Simplify 2 : 4.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Knowledge", "accept": ["1:2", "1:2", "1 : 2"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m6u12s1m02", "type": "short", "prompt": "Simplify 3 : 9.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Knowledge", "accept": ["1:3", "1:3", "1 : 3"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m6u12s1m03", "type": "num", "prompt": "1 : 2 = 4 : ?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 8, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m6u12s1m04", "type": "num", "prompt": "2 : 5 = ? : 10", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 4, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m6u12s1m05", "type": "short", "prompt": "Simplify 6 : 8.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Knowledge", "accept": ["3:4", "3:4", "3 : 4"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m6u12s1m06", "type": "short", "prompt": "3 red, 4 blue. Red : blue?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Knowledge", "accept": ["3:4", "3:4", "3 : 4"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}], "notes": "v4", "pdf": [{"book": "c6u12", "p0": 2, "p1": 5, "label": "pages 2–5", "title": "Lesson 12.1 notes · Ratio", "note": "The whole lesson as a document you can print, then Practice on paper with answers at the back.", "look": []}]}, {"id": "12.2", "title": "Direct proportion", "objs": ["O2"], "lesson": [{"k": "hook", "t": "Cookie recipe", "p": ["A recipe makes **12 cookies** with **150 g of butter**. You want to make **30 cookies**.", "How much butter do you need? Try it before you read on."]}, {"k": "recall", "t": "Multiplying and dividing", "p": ["150 ÷ 6 = 25."], "qq": {"id": "m6u12s2t01", "type": "num", "prompt": "12 pens cost $6. Cost of 1 pen ($)?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.5, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "0.50."}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "In proportion", "p": ["Two quantities are **in proportion** if they increase or decrease **at the same rate**: double the cookies → double the butter."], "table": {"head": ["Cookies", "12", "6", "30"], "rows": [["Butter (g)", "150", "75", "375"]]}, "p2": ["Halve: 6 cookies need 75 g. Then × 5: 30 cookies need **375 g**."]}, {"k": "idea", "t": "The unitary method", "p": ["Find the amount for **one**, then multiply: 1 cookie needs 150 ÷ 12 = 12.5 g, so 30 cookies need 12.5 × 30 = **375 g**.", "Use whichever is easier – a friendly step (like 6) or one item."]}, {"k": "try", "t": "Scale", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m6u12s2t02", "type": "num", "prompt": "4 tickets cost $28. Cost of 7 tickets ($)?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 49, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "1 ticket $7.", "reason": "49."}}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I solve a proportion problem?", "p": ["Step 1: Check the quantities change at the same rate.", "Step 2: Find the value for 1 (or a handy number).", "Step 3: Multiply up to the amount you need.", "Step 4: Check that the answer is sensible."]}, {"k": "example", "t": "Recipe", "p": [], "q": "3 eggs make 2 cakes. Eggs for 8 cakes?", "steps": [["× 4", ""], ["12 eggs", ""]], "a": "12"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Unitary", "p": [], "q": "5 kg of rice costs $7.50. Cost of 3 kg?", "steps": [["1 kg $1.50", ""], ["3 kg $4.50", ""]], "a": "$4.50"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Map", "p": [], "q": "2 cm on a map = 5 km. 14 cm = ?", "steps": [["× 7", ""], ["35 km", ""]], "a": "35 km"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Not in proportion", "p": [], "q": "A taxi costs $3 plus $2 per km. Is cost in proportion to distance?", "steps": [["1 km $5, 2 km $7 – doubling distance doesn't double cost", ""]], "a": "no"}, {"k": "try", "t": "Unitary", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m6u12s2t03", "type": "num", "prompt": "6 bottles cost $9. Cost of 10 ($)?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 15, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "15."}}, {"k": "error", "t": "Added instead of scaling", "p": ["Find the first wrong line."], "q": "12 cookies need 150 g butter. 24 cookies?", "lines": ["12 more cookies → 12 g more butter: 162 g"], "bad": 0, "why": "Twice the cookies need twice the butter: 300 g.", "fix": [["× 2 → 300 g", ""]], "id": "m6u12s2t04"}, {"k": "mistake", "t": "Adding the same amount instead of multiplying", "p": ["In proportion means multiply by the same factor."]}, {"k": "tip", "t": "Real life", "p": ["Cooks scale recipes, shops price by weight and maps scale distances using proportion."]}, {"k": "summary", "t": "What to remember", "p": ["In proportion: change at the same rate.", "Unitary method: find 1, then multiply.", "Or scale with a friendly factor.", "Check the answer is sensible."]}], "video": {"src": null, "offset": 0, "dur": 660, "range": ""}, "stops": [{"id": "12.2-k1", "t": 1, "after": 0, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id":